---
import Project from '../../layouts/Project.astro';

const repo =
	'https://github.com/buragapuravi/ravikumarburagapu.com/tree/main/india-agricultural-evidence-assistant';
---

<Project
	title="India Agricultural Evidence Assistant"
	description="A local, evidence-first agricultural research prototype with cited retrieval, structured data, and explicit abstention."
	tag="EVIDENCE-FIRST RAG · AGRICULTURE · RESEARCH PROTOTYPE"
	intro="Explore agricultural research documents with answers linked to source passages and pages. The prototype combines dense and lexical retrieval, optional reranking, and a deterministic evidence gate designed to abstain when support is insufficient."
	status="Local research demo · not an advisory service"
	stack="Python · Streamlit · LlamaIndex · Chroma · BM25"
	repo={repo}
>
	<section aria-labelledby="workflow">
		<h2 id="workflow">A traceable research workflow</h2>
		<p>
			Ask a question about the bundled research corpus, optionally
			narrow it by crop or location, and inspect the retrieved passages,
			source metadata, and retrieval trace behind the response. A
			bounded, opt-in research planner can suggest up to two follow-up
			searches while retaining the original question.
		</p>
		<p>
			Structured indicators and district comparisons use validated
			source rows rather than asking a language model to calculate
			numeric results. Responses validate cited source IDs and pages
			before they are displayed.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section aria-labelledby="safety">
		<h2 id="safety">Evidence boundaries matter</h2>
		<p>
			This is an evidence-discovery teaching prototype, not an
			official advisory service or a substitute for current government
			guidance, pesticide labels, institutional review, or local
			agronomists. The bundled documents are clearly labeled synthetic
			teaching fixtures and must never be used to make farming
			decisions. The app does not independently verify source
			authenticity or agronomic correctness.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section aria-labelledby="run">
		<h2 id="run">Run it locally</h2>
		<p>
			The project runs locally and can return cited extractive evidence
			without a paid API key. Model-backed synthesis and the bounded
			research planner are optional and require a configured local or
			OpenAI-compatible provider.
		</p>
		<pre><code>cd india-agricultural-evidence-assistant
python3.12 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e '.[dev]'
cp .env.example .env
python -m app.prepare_models
python -m app.ingest --input data/demo --input data/raw --rebuild
streamlit run streamlit_app.py --server.address 127.0.0.1 --server.port 8502</code></pre>
		<p>
			See the repository README for setup details, framework and storage
	options, evaluation methodology, and limitations.
		</p>
	</section>
</Project>
